<p>&#8220;A man of correct insight among those who are duped and deluded resembles one whose watch is right while all the clocks in the town give the wrong time. He alone knows the correct time, but of what use is this to him? The whole world is guided by the clocks that show the wrong time.&#8221; &#8212; Schopenhauer, <em>Counsels and Maxims</em></p>
